1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:04,404
Before any code, what actually happens when someone pays a shop online with a card?

2
00:00:04,404 --> 00:00:10,916
Five players are involved: the buyer, the shop, the acquirer bank, the processing center, and the issuer bank.

3
00:00:10,916 --> 00:00:17,535
The acquirer is the shop's bank, the one this series describes, and the issuer is the bank that gave the buyer their card.

4
00:00:17,535 --> 00:00:28,666
Every shop's website gets an e POS terminal for each card scheme, a virtual POS terminal identified by a merchant ID and a terminal ID, the MID and TID.

5
00:00:28,666 --> 00:00:34,440
When the buyer pays, the acquirer sends an authorization through the processing center to the issuer.

6
00:00:34,440 --> 00:00:40,869
Depending on the card scheme, the issuer either debits the money in a single step, or first places a hold on it.

7
00:00:40,869 --> 00:00:51,321
A hold is then captured, and only then is the payment final; every scheme, Uzcard and Humo today, Visa or Mastercard later, follows one of these two ways.

8
00:00:51,321 --> 00:00:56,702
A reversal cancels a payment before settlement, and a refund sends money back after it.

9
00:00:56,702 --> 00:01:01,166
At the end of the day, the processing center settles all payments with the acquirer.

10
00:01:01,166 --> 00:01:05,773
The acquirer keeps its commission and pays the shop the rest by the next banking day.

11
00:01:05,773 --> 00:01:14,392
These words, authorization, capture, MID, TID, and settlement, name the classes in every episode that follows.

